# Clinic Manager naming

When the user says **Clinic Manager**, they mean the role formerly called Branch Admin / Branch Manager / Franchise Owner.

## Canonical mapping

| Product / UI name | Internal / DB role id |
|---|---|
| **Clinic Manager** | `BRANCH_ADMIN` |

Do **not** rename the database role id `BRANCH_ADMIN` unless explicitly asked (RLS, seeds, and Auth rely on it).

DB `roles.description` for that id is **Clinic Manager** (migration `20261005000051_clinic_manager_role_label.sql`).

## When implementing

- User-facing labels, copy, cards, and dropdowns: **Clinic Manager**
- Use `formatRoleLabel()` from `src/utils/roleLabels.ts` for role display
- Code identifiers may still say `branchOwner`, `isBranchOwner`, `BRANCH_ADMIN`, etc.
- Dashboard / commission features for this role are **clinic-manager-only**, not HQ

## Language in replies

Prefer “clinic manager” over “branch admin” or “branch manager” when talking with the user.
